.TH BOSWAS-CALCULATOR 1 "November 2026" "Boswas OS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
boswas-calculator \- calculator with standard, scientific and programmer modes, date calculation and unit converters
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B boswas-calculator
.RB [ \-\-new\-window ]
.RB [ \-\-mode
.IR MODE ]
.br
.B boswas-calculator \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B boswas-calculator
is the calculator of Boswas OS. The menu at the top left switches between
.TP
.B Standard
The four operations, percent, reciprocal, square and square root. An
operation is carried out as soon as the next operator is pressed, so
2 + 3 \(mu 4 gives 20. Sixteen digits are shown.
.TP
.B Scientific
Operator precedence and parentheses, powers and roots, logarithms,
factorial (also of numbers that are not whole), the trigonometric and
hyperbolic functions and their inverses in degrees, radians or gradians,
and scientific notation (F\-E). Thirty\-two digits are shown.
.TP
.B Programmer
Whole numbers of 64, 32, 16 or 8 bits in two's complement, shown in
hexadecimal, decimal, octal and binary at once, with the bitwise operators,
arithmetic and logical shifts, rotation (also through the carry bit) and a
keypad that toggles single bits.
.TP
.B Date calculation
The difference between two dates in years, months, weeks and days, and a
date plus or minus years, months and days.
.TP
.B Converter
Length, weight and mass, temperature, area, volume, speed, time, data,
energy, power, pressure and angle. The factors are the exact definitions
of the units. There is no currency converter: the calculator never uses
the network.
.PP
Numbers are kept as exact fractions where the calculation allows it and to
42 significant digits otherwise, so 0.1 + 0.2 is 0.3 and 1 \(di 3 \(mu 3 is 1.
A calculation that has no result shows
.BR "Cannot divide by zero" ,
.BR "Result is undefined" ,
.B "Invalid input"
or
.B Overflow
(from 10^10000 on) and waits for
.BR C .
.PP
Standard and Scientific mode keep a history of the last twenty
calculations each; every calculator mode has a memory list (MS, MR, M+,
M\-, MC). Neither is kept after the program ends. The mode last used, the
angle unit, the word size and radix and the units of each converter are
remembered. Every start of the program opens its own window.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-new\-window
Open a new calculator. Every start of the program is a calculator of its own
(as in Windows), so this is what a plain start does too; the desktop entry's
\(lqNew Window\(rq action uses it.
.TP
.BI \-\-mode " MODE"
Open in
.I MODE
instead of the mode used last:
.BR standard ,
.BR scientific ,
.BR programmer ,
.B date
or a converter
.RB ( length ,
.BR weight ,
.BR temperature ,
.BR area ,
.BR volume ,
.BR speed ,
.BR time ,
.BR data ,
.BR energy ,
.BR power ,
.BR pressure ,
.BR angle ).
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a summary of the options and exit.
.SH KEYBOARD
.TP
.B Everywhere
Digits, + \- * /, Enter or = (equals), Esc (C), Delete (CE), Backspace,
F9 (change the sign), Ctrl+C and Ctrl+V (copy and paste the number;
pasted text that is not a number is refused), Ctrl+M (MS), Ctrl+P (M+),
Ctrl+Q (M\-), Ctrl+R (MR), Ctrl+L (MC), Ctrl+H (history), Ctrl+Shift+D
(clear the history), Alt+1 Standard, Alt+2 Scientific, Alt+3 Programmer,
Alt+4 Date calculation.
.TP
.B Standard
% (percent), R (reciprocal), Q (square), @ (square root).
.TP
.B Scientific
( and ), ^ or Y (power), Ctrl+Y (root), Q (square), # (cube), @ (square
root), ! (factorial), L (log), Shift+L (log to base y), N (ln), Ctrl+N
(e to the x), G (two to the x), Ctrl+G (ten to the x), P (pi), E (e),
X (exponent), V (F\-E), % or D (modulo), | (absolute value), [ (floor),
] (ceiling), M (degrees, minutes, seconds); S, O, T, U, I, J for sine,
cosine, tangent, secant, cosecant, cotangent, with Shift for the inverse
and Ctrl for the hyperbolic function; F3 degrees, F4 radians, F5 gradians.
.TP
.B Programmer
A to F (hexadecimal digits), & (AND), | (OR), ^ (XOR), ~ (NOT), . (NAND),
\e (NOR), < and > (shift), J and K (rotate), % (modulo), ( and ),
F5 hexadecimal, F6 decimal, F7 octal, F8 binary, F12 QWORD, F2 DWORD,
F3 WORD, F4 BYTE.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/com.boswas.Calculator/state.json
The mode used last and the choices of each mode.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/com.boswas.Calculator/window.ini
The size of the window.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when the window was closed; 2 for a wrong option; 4 when started as
root, which the program refuses.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR boswas\-text\-editor (1)
